Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 56, verse 49:

His saying, the Exalted: ﴿Say: Indeed, the former and the latter﴾ ﴿will surely be gathered to the appointed time of a known day.﴾

When the disbelievers denied their resurrection and that of their earliest forefathers in the previous verse, Allah commanded His Prophet ﷺ to inform them, with an emphatic statement, that the former and the latter, all of them, will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection for reckoning and recompense after their resurrection. (p-526)

What this noble verse includes regarding the resurrection of the former and the latter and their gathering on the Day of Resurrection has been clarified in many verses, such as:

• His saying: ﴿That is the Day of Gathering, the Day of Mutual Loss and Gain﴾ [At-Taghabun: 9];

• And His saying, the Exalted: ﴿Allah – there is no deity except Him. He will surely gather you into the Day of Resurrection﴾ [An-Nisa': 87];

• And His saying, the Exalted: ﴿Our Lord, You are the gatherer of the people for a Day about which there is no doubt﴾ [Ali 'Imran: 9], to the end of the verse;

• And His saying, the Exalted: ﴿That is a Day for which the people will be gathered﴾ [Hud: 103];

• And His saying, the Exalted: ﴿This is the Day of Decision; We have gathered you and the former peoples﴾ [Al-Mursalat: 38];

• And His saying, the Exalted: ﴿And We gathered them, and We left none of them behind﴾ [Al-Kahf: 47].

We have already presented this in detail in Surah al-Hijr, in the discussion of His saying, the Exalted: ﴿And We guarded it from every accursed devil﴾ [Al-Hijr: 17].
